    <!-- GeneralsX @feature Android port accent-colors 16/10/2026 The DARKMODE
         halves of the alternate accent palettes offered by the launcher's
         Interface -> Accent picker (ThemeHelper). The default violet lives in
         the base values-night/colors.xml and needs no overlay. Names mirror
         values/accent_colors.xml exactly - keep the two lists in sync.

         The surface ladder here is the accent's hue as a PALE DARK wash -
         near-black grounds carrying only a whisper of the hue (the violet
         dark palette in values-night/colors.xml is the reference: #0E0E11
         ground, #1A1A21 cards). Surfaces stay dim so the light on-accent
         tones and the neutral light text roles keep their contrast; the
         accent's own saturation lives in the primary/container roles, not
         in the walls. On-secondary follows the dark-mode convention (light
         on dark container). Dark outline stays near-neutral so hairlines
         read as structure, not colour. -->

    <!-- Blue -->
